NFR_COLS = ["ID", "Category", "Requirement"]
NFR = [
["NFR-01","Technology stack","Java 17; Jakarta Servlet 6.0 / JSP with JSTL 3.0 (MVC: Servlet – Service – DAO); Apache Tomcat 10.1; Microsoft SQL Server with mssql-jdbc 13.4; jBCrypt 0.4 for password hashing; Gson 2.11 for JSON; Angus Mail 2.0 (SMTP) for email; Apache POI 5.3 for Excel export; JUnit 5 and Mockito 5 for unit tests; Maven build; Git / GitHub for source control. Background jobs run on the JDK scheduler inside the application (no extra library)."],
["NFR-02","External services","VNPay payment gateway (sandbox) for online payment (API-01, API-02); an SMTP mailbox for verification codes, temporary passwords and alerts (API-03); Open-Meteo for the PT dashboard weather (API-04); wger.de public exercise API for the Exercise Library (API-05). When an external service is unavailable the related feature shows an error message (or its last cached data) and the rest of the system keeps working."],
["NFR-03","Usability","The interface is in Vietnamese; dates dd/mm/yyyy, times 24-hour, money in VND with thousand separators (GBR-01, GBR-02, GBR-29). Every error is a message from section System Messages, shown next to the field it concerns or as a toast (GBR-17). Each main screen has an (i) hint box for its explanations instead of a subtitle line (GBR-36). Texts shown to users never contain rule codes (GBR-37). Statuses always have a text label besides their colour (GBR-28)."],
["NFR-04","Compatibility","The web application is used on current versions of Chrome, Edge and Firefox. Every main screen is usable at 390 px (phone), 768 / 1024 px (tablet) and 1440 px (desktop) without horizontal page scrolling (GBR-35); calendars switch to a one-day or list view on narrow screens. Light and dark themes keep readable contrast."],
["NFR-05","Security","Passwords and temporary passwords are stored only as BCrypt hashes and are never shown or logged (DBR-02). Every page except the public pages, Sign In, Register and Forgot Password requires sign-in, and every request is checked against the role the user is working in (GBR-10, GBR-13). Every POST made while signed in carries a CSRF token that is checked on the server (MSG214); the only POSTs without it are Sign In, Register, Forgot Password and the VNPay IPN, which is verified by its signature instead. A sign-in session expires after 2 hours without activity (GBR-31); a password change or reset signs out the other sessions (CBR-93). Database access uses parameterised queries only; sort and filter values are taken from fixed lists. All output is HTML-escaped. Uploaded images are JPG or PNG up to 5 MB and 2000 px."],
["NFR-06","Data integrity and retention","No business record is physically deleted except the cases listed in GBR-05. A deleted customer profile keeps its row as Inactive together with its orders, transactions, subscriptions, check-ins and sessions, so revenue and tax records stay complete. Every multi-step change (sale, payment, session handling, publishing slots, leave decision, maintenance decision) runs in one database transaction with its audit line (GBR-07, GBR-08); concurrent changes are resolved by locks and conditional updates (GBR-13, GBR-32)."],
["NFR-07","Performance","Under normal use at one gym, a screen opens and a save completes within a few seconds. Filtering, counting, sorting and paging are done in SQL, never by loading whole tables; page sizes per screen follow GBR-18."],
["NFR-08","Constraints","The system serves one gym in one time zone (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh). There is no SMS, no mobile app, no e-invoice and no in-system refund; these are handled outside the system (GBR-15, GBR-16). Daily background jobs run at 00:05 and minute jobs run every minute (GBR-14)."],
["NFR-09","Reliability of background jobs","Each background job processes records one by one in separate transactions, so one failing record does not stop the others. A daily job that hits a database error is retried every 5 minutes; jobs are idempotent (running twice changes nothing more, e.g. JOB-08 never sends the same reminder twice)."],
["NFR-10","Accessibility","Every action can be done with the keyboard (Tab, Enter, Space, Escape closes dialogs and hint boxes and returns focus); icons have text alternatives; dialogs trap focus; on a small screen icon-only buttons keep their accessible names."],
]
